# DESYNAR DESIGN SYSTEM

### (Atelier Principles → Practical Rules)

---

# 1️⃣ Design Philosophy Rule

**Principle:** Craft over clutter.

**Rule:**

- Every screen must have a single primary action.
- Maximum 3 visual focal points per screen.
- No decorative UI elements without functional purpose.

If it does not serve clarity or brand elevation → remove it.

---

# 2️⃣ Layout System Rules

### Spacing Grid

Use a strict 8pt spacing system:

- 8 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48 / 64
- No random margins.
- No uneven paddings.

### Vertical Rhythm

- Headline → 24–32px spacing
- Section → 48–64px separation
- Button stack spacing → 16–24px

Luxury = breathing room.

---

# 3️⃣ Typography System

## Font Pairing Structure

**Primary Display (Emotional)**

- Use metropolis font headings
- Used only for:
  - Taglines
  - Hero headlines
  - Editorial moments

**UI Font (Functional)**

- Use appropriate metropolis font weight
- Used for:
  - Buttons
  - Labels
  - Inputs
  - Navigation

---

## Typography Hierarchy

| Level | Use Case         | Weight           | Purpose          |
| ----- | ---------------- | ---------------- | ---------------- |
| H1    | Editorial hero   | Medium / Regular | Emotional anchor |
| H2    | Section titles   | Medium           | Structure        |
| Body  | Descriptions     | Regular          | Readability      |
| Label | Inputs / Buttons | Medium           | Clarity          |

No ultra-bold unless for CTA.

---

# 4️⃣ Color System Rules

## Core Palette (Dark Luxury Mode)

Primary Background:
Use primary 500 variant

Surface Panel:
Use secondary 100 variant

Primary Text:
Use primary 500

Muted Text:
`#A1A1A1`

Accent (Gold):
`#C6A75E`

---

## Rules

- Accent color only used for:
  - Active states
  - Highlights
  - Micro indicators

- Never use more than 1 accent color per screen.
- Avoid high-saturation colors.

Luxury = controlled palette.

---

# 5️⃣ Surface & Depth Rules

### Panels

- Border radius: 20–28px
- Soft shadow only (no hard shadows)
- Subtle elevation difference between background and panel

### Glass Effects

- Backdrop blur max 20px
- Opacity between 70–85%
- No heavy frosted gimmicks

Depth must be subtle, not trendy.

---

# 6️⃣ Button System

### Primary Button

- High contrast fill
- Full width on mobile
- Height: 48–56px
- Radius: 16–20px
- Slight press animation (scale 0.97)

### Secondary Button

- Outline style
- Same height
- No heavy borders (1px max)

### Rules

- One primary CTA per screen.
- No double-primary buttons.

---

# 7️⃣ Motion System

Luxury motion is restrained.

### Timing

- 200–300ms
- Ease-in-out

### Animations

- Fade
- Slide (subtle)
- Scale (micro press only)

No bounce.
No overshoot.
No playful spring.

---

# 8️⃣ Imagery Rules

If background imagery is used:

- Must relate to tailoring, craftsmanship, or fabric.
- Slightly desaturated.
- Dark overlay for readability.
- Never busy or colorful.

Imagery supports atmosphere, not distraction.

---

# 9️⃣ Content Tone Rules

Replace generic SaaS language.

Avoid:

- “Welcome back”
- “Get started”
- “Continue”

Prefer:

- “Enter”
- “Continue with Google”
- “Create your account”
- “Curated tailoring.”

Language should feel intentional and curated.

---

# 🔟 Component Constraints

To maintain atelier discipline:

- Max 5 components per screen section.
- No more than 2 font sizes per section.
- No more than 3 colors per section.

Constraint builds identity.

---

# 11️⃣ Accessibility Rule (Enterprise Requirement)

Luxury does not excuse poor usability.

- Minimum contrast ratio: 4.5:1
- Tap targets: minimum 44px height
- Focus states visible
- Motion can be reduced (respect OS settings)

---

# What This Achieves for Desynar

It ensures:

- Every screen feels curated.
- Brand identity remains consistent.
- Developers have fixed rules.
- Design decisions become repeatable.
- The UI feels intentional, not assembled.

---

# Summary

Atelier → Craft → Restraint → Structure → System.

When translated properly:

It becomes a disciplined, premium design language — not just a visual mood.
